'''Juno''' ([[minor-planet designation]]: '''3 Juno''') is a large [[asteroid]] in the [[asteroid belt]]. Juno was the third asteroid discovered, in 1804, by German astronomer [[Karl Ludwig Harding|Karl Harding]].<ref>{{Citation |author1=Cunningham |first=Clifford J |title=Bode's Law and the Discovery of Juno: Historical Studies in Asteroid Research |date=2017 |publisher=Springer |isbn=978-3-319-32875-1}}</ref> It is [[List of exceptional asteroids|tied with three other asteroids as the thirteenth largest asteroid]], and it is one of the two largest stony ([[S-type asteroid|S-type]]) asteroids, along with [[15 Eunomia]]. It is estimated to contain 1% of the total mass of the asteroid belt.<ref name="Pitjeva05">
